     FateBank.pic and the FILE_ID.DIZ. Adding of BBS Adverts to the
     FILE_ID.DIZ is lame.


WHAT'S IT?
==========

     I was asked to make a Program in which Users could save their Time
     into a sort of Bank. When they would need Time in the Future, e.g.
     to completely download a File, they just got it from the TimeBank.
     I was also asked to make a Program in which Users who needed just
     few KBytes to download Program could spend some Online Time for
     the missing Credits. Or some of his File Credits.

     FateBank combines this all into one Program. It handles the User's
     Time left, Time saved on FateBank's Account, the User's File and
     the User's Byte Credits. In fact FateBank allows you to:

     - store Time on your Account
     - withdraw Time from your Account
     - convert Time to File or Byte Credits
     - convert File or Byte Credits to Time
     - convert Byte to File Credits
     - convert File to Byte Credits


FEATURES
========

     + Multi-Purpose Utility
     + Exchange Ratios are configurable - without Configfile
     + Does not use any Datafile but stores Data in User Structure
     + While using FateBank the User's Timer is disabled
     + Cursor-Movement Routines
     + Backdoors :)
     + Easy to use

     Take a Look at "FateBank.pic"!


GLOSSARY
========

     Before you read on the following Things should be clear:

     Saved Time:         is the Time a User once saved into his FateBank
                         Account which can be withdrawn at any Time or
                         converted to File or Byte Credits.
     Time left:          is the Time a User has left for this Call.
                         After leaving FateBank this Value gets reduced,
                         not while online.
     Exchange Ratios:    FateBank doesn't convert one Minute to one KByte.
                         It's *you* who defines how much Bytes the User
                         gets when he converts one Minute. You specify
                         this Relation through an Exchange Ratio.


INSTALLATION
============

     Nothing easier than that. Just move FateBank somewhere in your
     PFiles: Directory and load up your favourite Texteditor for...


CONFIGURATION
=============

     FateBank stores the saved Time unlike other TimeBanks not in a
     Datafile but in a currently unused Part of the User Structure
     which is not editable by Edit Account. However you may have
     Tools installed which use this Location. Also, CNet maybe uses
     this Location in future Versions. Therefore, to prevent corrupt
     Data, you can alter the Location. The default Location is 1400406.
     Alternative Locations are 1500428, 1200450, 1400672, 1400676 and
     1300730. These Locations aren't safe either! You have to test them.
     It *is* possible that some of these Locations are used in my later
     Tools. Of course, I'll then write it into their Docfiles.
     The Variable guloc specifies the GetUser Location for FateBank.

     Then there are the Exchange Ratios. Here are the they:
     - Variable fc2t
     - Variable bc2t
     - Variable bc2fc

     The Variable fc2t defines how much File Credits you need to get
     one Minute of Time et vice versa. Default is one.

     The Variable bc2t defines how much Byte Credits you need to get
     one Minute of Time et vice versa. Default is 5120 (5KB).

     The Variable bc2fc defines how much Byte Credits you need to get
     one File Credit. Default is 10240 (10KB).

     C'est tout.

USAGE
=====

     FateBank is controlled using the Cursor-Keys. The Main Menu:

     Time saved Time left File Credits Byte Credits Backdoors About Quit

     Select one of the first four you want to be increased. You'll then be
     prompted where you wish to get the Time from. Examples:
     - to get 4 Minutes of Time from the stored Time
       Press Enter at "Time left". Select "Time saved" and press 4x Enter.
     - to get 2 File Credits from Byte Credits
       Press Enter at "File Credits". Select "Byte Credits" and press 2x
       Enter.

     The Functions won't work if you don't have enough Time or Credits.
     Also FateBank has some internal Limits. You can store max. 999 Mins.
     You must have at least 3 Minutes left, 2*fc2t File Credits and
     2*bc2t Byte Credits. If you use the Standard Values you must have
     at least 2 File Credits and 20480 Byte Credits.
     
     Backdoors brings you to a Menu of Pseudo-Backdoors. These won't cause
     any Damage, they were implemented "just for fun".
     Note: The Backdoor "Download Userdata" doesn't work on a local Port.
     Try it remote or on a Nullmodem Port.

     About brings you to a nice Screen with Copyright Remarks, Ways how
     you can contact me and Greetings.

     Quit brings you back to good, old CNet.


ERROR-SAFETY
============

     I tried to make FateBank safe against all Kinds of Errors. FateBank
     handles Carrier Dumpers as well as the "HI" Commando as well as
     Syntax Errors though it should be bug-free. Also if the GetUser
     appears to be in use FateBank will notify you.


